# Line-ending policy.
#
# The repo is worked on from Windows and Linux. Without this file a Windows
# checkout rewrites LF to CRLF, and every file then shows as fully modified:
# docker-compose.yml alone produced 78 changed lines for zero content change.
# That makes diffs unreviewable and causes conflicts on files nobody edited.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: git decides what is text, stores it with LF in the
# repository, and checks it out with LF everywhere. Editors on Windows handle
# LF fine; the CRLF round-trip is what caused the churn.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries - never touched, never diffed as text.
*.db     binary
*.joblib binary
*.parquet binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.docx   binary
*.zip    binary

# Notebooks are JSON, so they are text, but a line-by-line diff of one is
# noise. Mark them so `git diff` says "binary" rather than printing 4,000 lines.
*.ipynb  -diff

# Scripts that must keep LF even if someone forces CRLF elsewhere.
Makefile text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
